faqs:
  - question: Do you repair gutters or just replace them?
    answer: "<p>We repair them when repair is the honest answer. If your gutters are fundamentally sound and it's one bad spot — a leaking seam, a sagging run, a few loose hangers — we'll tell you that and repair it. If they're sectional gutters past twelve to fifteen years old with more than one seam leaking, patching usually buys two or three years before you're calling again, and replacement makes more sense. And if a gutter is sagging because the fascia behind it is rotten, the real repair is the wood: we fix the fascia first so the hangers have something solid to grip.</p>"
  - question: How much does gutter repair cost in Huntsville?
    answer: "<p>It depends on what's actually wrong, which is why we start with a free inspection instead of a phone quote. A sagging gutter might just need to be re-secured, or it might be hanging on rotten fascia that has to be replaced first — those are very different jobs. We'll show you exactly what we find and give you an exact quote before any work begins. If fascia is part of the repair, it typically runs $5-15 per linear foot in Huntsville, and most homes need 10-40 feet replaced.</p>"
