  - question: How do I know if my fascia is rotted?
    answer: "<p>Signs of fascia damage include: paint peeling or bubbling, soft or spongy wood when pressed, visible dark staining or discoloration, gutters pulling away from the house, or gaps between fascia and soffit. We inspect fascia as part of every gutter estimate — many homeowners don't know they have damage until we point it out.</p>"
  - question: Can you repair fascia without replacing gutters?
