{% set local_problem %}
<p>Alabama's humidity is brutal on exposed wood — and Huntsville is no exception. When gutters clog, leak at seams, or overflow during heavy rains, water runs behind them and soaks into the fascia boards. In Huntsville's climate, that moisture doesn't dry out quickly. Instead, it creates perfect conditions for rot, mold, and wood-destroying insects.</p>

<p>We see this constantly: homeowners call about new gutters or a gutter repair — a sagging run, a leaking seam — but when we inspect their homes, we find fascia that's soft, water-stained, or visibly rotting behind the existing gutters. Installing new gutters on damaged wood is pointless — they won't stay securely attached, and the underlying damage will continue spreading.</p>

<p>Huntsville's mix of housing stock creates different fascia challenges. Historic homes in Five Points and Twickenham often have original wood fascia that's weathered decades of exposure. Meanwhile, homes built during the 2000s-2010s construction boom in Hampton Cove, Jones Valley, and South Huntsville frequently used lower-quality materials — OSB or thin composite boards that weren't designed for Alabama's moisture levels.</p>

<p>The good news: caught early, fascia repair is straightforward and relatively affordable. Left alone, rot spreads to rafters, roof sheathing, and structural components — turning a $500 repair into a $5,000+ problem.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>We start with a thorough inspection, checking fascia and soffit for water damage, soft spots, and rot. We'll show you exactly what we find and explain what needs repair — no hidden damage, no surprise charges later.</p>

<p>For damaged sections, we carefully remove existing gutters, cut out the rotted wood back to solid material, and install new fascia boards. We use quality primed lumber or composite materials specifically designed for exterior exposure in humid climates like Huntsville's.</p>

<p>Everything is properly sealed, caulked, and prepared for new gutter installation. Then we install your new seamless gutters on the fresh fascia — properly attached with appropriate hangers, properly sloped for drainage, and designed to prevent the overflow that caused the rot in the first place.</p>

<p>You get a complete solution from one contractor: carpentry, gutters, and the peace of mind that comes from knowing the job was done right.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We've been repairing fascia, repairing gutters, and installing new ones throughout Huntsville for over 20 years. We understand that these two jobs are inseparable — you can't have reliable gutters without solid fascia to mount them on, and you can't protect fascia without properly functioning gutters to keep water away from it.</p>

<p>Our crews handle both carpentry and gutter installation, which means better coordination, cleaner work, and a single point of accountability. We're not going to blame the "other guy" if something goes wrong. When we're done, your home is fully protected from roof edge to foundation — backed by our warranty and our 20+ year reputation in Huntsville.</p>
{% endset %}

